msgid "ui.chapter.50.intro"
msgstr "An interpolated tale about a test of trust that goes wrong."

msgid "ui.chapter.50.title"
msgstr "The Curious Impertinent"

msgid "ui.chapter.48.intro"
msgstr "They come home and he begins to recover his senses."

msgid "ui.chapter.48.title"
msgstr "Return to the Village"

msgid "ui.chapter.47.intro"
msgstr "They bid farewell to the Duke and Duchess."

msgid "ui.chapter.47.title"
msgstr "The Farewell"

msgid "ui.chapter.46.intro"
msgstr "Lions are displayed at court; Quixote observes them."

msgid "ui.chapter.46.title"
msgstr "The Lions at Court"

msgid "ui.chapter.45.intro"
msgstr "Sancho is enchanted as part of Dulcinea's disenchantment."

msgid "ui.chapter.45.title"
msgstr "Sancho Enchanted"

msgid "ui.chapter.44.intro"
msgstr "A fight with the white moon knight is somehow avoided."

msgid "ui.chapter.44.title"
msgstr "Duels Avoided"

msgid "ui.chapter.43.intro"
msgstr "A criminal case is brought before the Duke; Quixote judges it."

msgid "ui.chapter.43.title"
msgstr "The Criminal Case"

msgid "ui.chapter.42.intro"
msgstr "The puppets perform Moors, and Quixote attacks them."

msgid "ui.chapter.42.title"
msgstr "Maestro Pedro's Puppet Show"

msgid "ui.chapter.41.intro"
msgstr "A canon argues with him about a false sequel."

msgid "ui.chapter.41.title"
msgstr "Oviedo's False Book"

msgid "ui.chapter.40.intro"
msgstr "They come upon a rich man's burial procession."

msgid "ui.chapter.40.title"
msgstr "The Burial of the Rich Man"

msgid "ui.chapter.39.intro"
msgstr "Sancho takes up his governorship of the ínsula Barataria."

msgid "ui.chapter.39.title"
msgstr "Sancho as Governor"

msgid "ui.chapter.38.intro"
msgstr "A wooden horse carries them on a flight that never leaves the ground."

msgid "ui.chapter.38.title"
msgstr "Clavileño"

msgid "ui.chapter.37.intro"
msgstr "The Duchess pretends to be enchanted and enlists Sancho."

msgid "ui.chapter.37.title"
msgstr "The Duchess's Enchantment"

msgid "ui.chapter.36.intro"
msgstr "Sancho tends his wounds after the defeat."

msgid "ui.chapter.36.title"
msgstr "Sancho's Care"

msgid "ui.chapter.35.intro"
msgstr "A rival defeats him and sends him home for a year."

msgid "ui.chapter.35.title"
msgstr "The Knight of the White Moon"

msgid "ui.chapter.34.intro"
msgstr "A tale of woe leads on to the wooden horse."

msgid "ui.chapter.34.title"
msgstr "The Enchantment"

msgid "ui.chapter.33.intro"
msgstr "Two lions are brought out at the Duke's castle."

msgid "ui.chapter.33.title"
msgstr "The Lions at the Castle"

msgid "ui.chapter.32.intro"
msgstr "The Duke welcomes them as guests. Guests are not equals."

msgid "ui.chapter.32.title"
msgstr "The Duke's Castle"

msgid "ui.chapter.31.intro"
msgstr "He returns to the cave where he had his vision."

msgid "ui.chapter.31.title"
msgstr "Back to the Cave"

msgid "ui.chapter.30.intro"
msgstr "A cart of lions crosses the road and he challenges them."

msgid "ui.chapter.30.title"
msgstr "The Lions on the Road"

msgid "ui.chapter.29.intro"
msgstr "Penitents are taken for criminals; their muleteers object."

msgid "ui.chapter.29.title"
msgstr "The Penitents in White"

msgid "ui.chapter.28.intro"
msgstr "A page promises to disenchant Dulcinea. Promise, not result."

msgid "ui.chapter.28.title"
msgstr "Dulcinea Disenchanted"

msgid "ui.chapter.27.intro"
msgstr "The fulling mills are taken for yet another enchantment."

msgid "ui.chapter.27.title"
msgstr "The Fulling Mills"

msgid "ui.chapter.26.intro"
msgstr "Master Pedro's puppets are attacked as if they were real."

msgid "ui.chapter.26.title"
msgstr "Melisendra's Puppet Show"

msgid "ui.chapter.25.intro"
msgstr "A tale of woe is told, and Altisidora takes her revenge."

msgid "ui.chapter.25.title"
msgstr "The Countess Trifaldi"

msgid "ui.chapter.24.intro"
msgstr "A lovesick maiden sings to him; songs are a kind of siege."

msgid "ui.chapter.24.title"
msgstr "Altisidora"

msgid "ui.chapter.23.intro"
msgstr "He descends into the cave and comes back with a tale."

msgid "ui.chapter.23.title"
msgstr "The Cave of Montesinos"

msgid "ui.chapter.22.intro"
msgstr "He fights the Knight of the Mirrors under a full moon."

msgid "ui.chapter.22.title"
msgstr "The Moonlight Duel"

msgid "ui.chapter.20.intro"
msgstr "A peasant girl is passed off as an enchanted Dulcinea, and he believes it."

msgid "ui.chapter.20.title"
msgstr "Dulcinea Enchanted"

msgid "ui.chapter.18.intro"
msgstr "The curate and the barber burn the books that made him."

msgid "ui.chapter.18.title"
msgstr "The Bonfire of Books"

msgid "ui.chapter.17.intro"
msgstr "Another body, another vengeance; Sancho talks him down again."

msgid "ui.chapter.17.title"
msgstr "The Dead Man, Again"

msgid "ui.chapter.16.intro"
msgstr "An enchanted boat waits on the river. Sancho does not believe in it."

msgid "ui.chapter.16.title"
msgstr "The Enchanted Boat"

msgid "ui.chapter.15.intro"
msgstr "A murdered man by the road; justice is argued out of existence."

msgid "ui.chapter.15.title"
msgstr "The Dead Man on the Road"

msgid "ui.chapter.14.intro"
msgstr "He frees the slaves and is stoned for his trouble."

msgid "ui.chapter.14.title"
msgstr "The Galley Slaves"

msgid "ui.chapter.13.intro"
msgstr "A joke staged as a court, and only one party is laughing."

msgid "ui.chapter.12.intro"
msgstr "Knowing the trick does not make it stop working."

msgid "ui.chapter.11.intro"
msgstr "An imitation fights you with your own moveset."

msgid "ui.chapter.10.intro"
msgstr "The outcome belongs to the test you designed, not to the world."

msgid "ui.chapter.09.intro"
msgstr "You choose who is tested, who tests, and what is at stake."

msgid "ui.chapter.08.intro"
msgstr "A case of confused speech, and not a single blow struck."

msgid "ui.chapter.07.intro"
msgstr "A name called across a field becomes a lady nobody can reach."

msgid "ui.chapter.06.intro"
msgstr "The thing that charges at them turns out to be sheep."

msgid "ui.chapter.05.intro"
msgstr "He enters a cave and returns with a vision no one can check."

msgid "ui.chapter.04.intro"
msgstr "A beating is read as an enchantment on the road to Montiel."

msgid "ui.chapter.03.intro"
msgstr "He frees the galley slaves; they answer him with stones."

msgid "ui.chapter.02.intro"
msgstr "A bargain made at an inn becomes a question of honour."

msgid "ui.chapter.01.intro"
msgstr "A mill in the field refuses to be only a mill."

msgid "ui.colofon.hint"
msgstr "Press any key to continue."

msgid "ui.colofon.title"
msgstr "Colophon — %s"

msgid "ui.colofon.el_castillo_del_duque.reality"
msgstr "It was a joke. Two people staged it and one of them paid for it. The castle is empty again; the cost is not."

msgid "ui.colofon.el_castillo_del_duque.book"
msgstr "The duke laughed and the world laughed with him. You may leave now, but you will keep asking who was the joke. That question is the last page."

msgid "ui.colofon.los_riscos.reality"
msgstr "Nobody made you stage that test. You chose who was told and what was at stake, and then watched the outcome as if it had happened to someone else."

msgid "ui.colofon.los_riscos.book"
msgstr "You built the test yourself and then were surprised by its ending. The world has no grudge against you. It simply kept the rules you wrote."

msgid "ui.colofon.el_toboso.reality"
msgstr "The girl never agreed to be a lady. You called her one from across a field, and the field carried your voice farther than you meant."

msgid "ui.colofon.el_toboso.book"
msgstr "You gave a name to a girl and the world made her a lady. Be careful with names: the world keeps them longer than the people who invented them."

msgid "ui.colofon.sierra_morena.reality"
msgstr "The cave was a hole in a hill. You went in frightened and came out needing to be believed. The mountain did not change; your need did."

msgid "ui.colofon.sierra_morena.book"
msgstr "The mountain kept its caves for those who could read them. You went down into one and came back with a vision nobody can disprove. That is enough."

msgid "ui.colofon.camino_la_mancha.reality"
msgstr "There were no giants in the field. There was dust, and a man who needed one. You did not discover the windmills — you decided what they were, and the decision outlived the road."

msgid "ui.colofon.camino_la_mancha.book"
msgstr "You believed the field was enchanted, and so it was. The windmills kept their secret until you gave them a name worth fighting. Turn the page: the road keeps what you made of it."

msgid "ui.colofon.prologo.reality"
msgstr "This book was written by a man who wanted to be read. You are only the latest person to hold it."

msgid "ui.colofon.prologo.book"
msgstr "This book was written to be read by you. Every page you turn makes it more true."

msgid "ui.chapter.ride"
msgstr "Riding to the next chapter…"

msgid "ui.region.camino_la_mancha.book"
msgstr "Endless fields, and a giant behind every windmill. The road to the first inn is paved with promises."
#. META: namespace=ui
msgid "ui.region.camino_la_mancha.reality"
msgstr "Wheat, dust, and windmills that are only windmills. The inn keeps a bed and a shelf of books nobody has read."
#. META: namespace=ui
msgid "ui.region.sierra_morena.book"
msgstr "A wall of dry mountain where every cave mouths a spell and every bandit is an enchanted knight."
#. META: namespace=ui
msgid "ui.region.sierra_morena.reality"
msgstr "Bare rock, heat, and the mouth of a cave that smells of sweat and incense. Bandits wait where the road narrows."
#. META: namespace=ui
msgid "ui.region.el_toboso.book"
msgstr "A village under a spell, where a peasant girl is a lady and the river runs with enchanted light."
#. META: namespace=ui
msgid "ui.region.el_toboso.reality"
msgstr "Slow water, low houses, and a girl who does not know she has been named. The village is ordinary; only he is not."
#. META: namespace=ui
msgid "ui.region.los_riscos.book"
msgstr "Sheer cliffs and a Gothic church where a man may put a whole world on trial."
#. META: namespace=ui
msgid "ui.region.los_riscos.reality"
msgstr "Fog in the rocks, a church of cold stone, and a scholar who has written a book about a knife."
#. META: namespace=ui
msgid "ui.region.el_castillo_del_duque.book"
msgstr "Silk, mirrors, and a duke who stages chivalry as theatre. Every corridor is a set; every servant is in on the joke."
#. META: namespace=ui
msgid "ui.region.el_castillo_del_duque.reality"
msgstr "A cold castle with gilded rooms, a bored duke, and two people who have decided to believe his lies."

